# Catalog-Only Work Item Mapping

Applies to `/generate-user-stories-from-transcript`, **work-item-mapping-agent**, **business-analyst-agent** mode `transcript-ado-csv`, `scripts/map-user-stories-to-sow-features.py` (default), and related subagents (`work-item-hierarchy-matcher`, `transcript-story-extractor`).

## Do

- When `work_item_mapping.feature_source` is `sow_json` (default): load **only** `artifacts/work-items/SOW.json` for Feature rows. **Ignore** `epic.json` and `feature.json` for transcript user-story mapping.
- After CSV validation PASS, spawn **work-item-mapping-agent** by explicit name every run; run `map-user-stories-to-sow-features.py` with thresholds from config (`strong_threshold`, `winner_margin`, `max_related_features`).
- SOW Feature row: Title 2 = `<Annexure ID minutes> - <BPM topic>`, Description = BPM topic, `ID` blank, `Annexure ID1` = minutes. No Epic rows.
- Match with **generic** title/description token overlap and optional `prerequisite_refs` → `WS-CE-*` from row JSON. Allow multiple User Story copies (up to `max_related_features`) when scores are within `winner_margin`.
- Public Excel row order: Workshop → SOW Features (with stories) in SOW.json order → unmatched User Stories → Issue/Risk. User Story `ID` stays blank.
- Register Open DQ when `SOW.json` is missing or has no `rows[]` — still deliver working CSV and INVEST scorecard; Excel may omit Feature hierarchy.
- Legacy ADO catalog mapping (`map-user-stories-to-work-items.py` + epic/feature JSON) applies only when config explicitly sets `feature_source: ado_catalog`.

## Don't

- Hardcode domain phrases, epic ID lists, topic hint tables, or finance/GL/B2B routing in agents, skills, or the mapper script.
- Invent Epic or Feature titles or IDs from the transcript; promote Workshop rows to Feature headers; add `EPIC ID` / `FEATURE ID` columns.
- Let business-analyst-agent fill catalog Feature `ID` on the public Excel — mapping is Phase 5 only.
- Skip work-item-mapping-agent because other JSON exists under `artifacts/work-items/` (e.g. validation reports, schema profiles).

